            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can emphasize (aka italicize) a word or phrase by enclosing it in a single pair of underscores (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "_word_"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") (constrained). You can emphasize bounded characters (i.e., characters within a word) by enclosing them in a pair of double underscores (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "char__act__ers"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") (unconstrained)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": "ex-italic",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An italic _word_, and an italic _phrase of text_.\n\nItalic c__hara__cter__s__ within a word."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Italic inline formatting"
